  "scope": [
    "The Windows journal contract runs on actual protected storage and leases; native host/process and recovery-verifier evidence is explicitly doubled in journal cases.",
    "Actual Windows original-worker process reinspection with held executable identity; protected registry target preparation and logical client registration preserve the reviewed load and allow metadata after channel close.",
    "A logical editor on the actual Job-backed synthetic app-server reuses the retained initialization response; stopping it leaves the original task metadata connection alive.",
    "Separate configuration and task Jobs run actual CodexClient initialization/account/read/resume against a synthetic app-server; saved scope and helper digest independently verify retirement.",
    "Protected registry, one-use review and no-replay checks use explicit provider/transport doubles on Windows.",
    "Exact owned Node fixture PID, birth, held executable file identity and SHA-256, current user and session.",
    "Exact established loopback TCP tuple; wrong client PID, reversed tuple and closed connection refuse.",
    "Original supervised helper exit and QUERY mask 8.",
    "Actual Windows Job-owned bidirectional byte stream with original guardian/worker checkpoints.",
    "Abrupt guardian loss retires its worker and descendant; blocked worker input and unacknowledged output retire on parent stop.",
    "Authenticated WebSocket upgrade and bidirectional JSON with an owned Windows Node process; original socket and helper retirement."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Composed task-protocol cases use explicit provider and process-query doubles; the separate carrier case uses actual Windows process queries.",
    "The later durable query-helper checkpoint callbacks are outside this source; native lifecycle/recovery, Suite editor connection and VS Code integration remain unfinished.",
